; The variable is visible_characters (with visible_ratio and visible_characters_behavior). No existing RichTextLabel
; scene sets any of them, so each drew the whole text before and draws it now: none can regress.
; One RichTextLabel per case, over the same 44-character text. Before Shaping (the default) shapes only
; the shown prefix, so its second line wraps again as the count grows (rich_text_label.cpp:668-671).
; After Shaping and the Glyphs behaviours keep the full wrap and skip glyphs (:943-947,1466). The
; paragraph labels cut BBCode text and show nothing at 0. The last two labels show that the default
; font joins `fi` into one glyph, so nine glyphs set the limit, and that `ft` stays two (:8017-8033).

